    body: '<p>Zürich Barracudas 3 finished the TOP 6 round on a high Wednesday night at Heerenschürli, defeating Zürich Challengers 8–7 in a tense one-run city derby. Challengers scored twice in each of the first two innings, but BAR3 answered one run at a time: Kelvis Garcia drove in Juan Malchans in the first, Wilkin Peguero doubled and scored in the second, and Jose Medina came home in the third to cut the deficit to 4–3.</p><p>The decisive swing came in the fourth. Peguero opened with a single, Carlos Moreno reached on a bunt and both advanced before Elvis Del Valle brought Peguero home. Malchans followed with an RBI single and Jhomar Rosa added a sacrifice fly, completing a three-run inning that put BAR3 ahead 6–4. The Cudas added two crucial insurance runs in the fifth: Moreno drove in Yohandris Pedroso on a groundout, then Del Valle doubled to center to score Sascha Litscher for an 8–4 lead.</p><p>Angel Elias held Challengers scoreless from the third through the sixth inning and earned the win. The visitors made one final push in the seventh, collecting four hits and three runs to close within 8–7. With the tying run still on base, Hansel Rodriguez induced Simon Steffen’s ground ball to third; the force at second ended the rally and the game.</p><p>The victory was BAR3’s third in a row and lifted the team to a 4–6 TOP 6 record. BAR3 now turns its attention to the NLA playoff semifinal against Therwil Flyers: Game 1 is Saturday, August 22 at 11:00 at Therwil Ballpark K1, followed by Game 2 on Sunday at 11:00 in Hünenberg.</p>',
